From d0563a71dc95b44c429a08a79b4c9a74f929bf59 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 7 Sep 2026 10:42:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: Pile-On preview and manual enrollment via chat
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Same discipline as chat-winback.ts's enrollProspectInWinBack: a
deliberately separate, simpler path from the production webhook handler
(handleInboundBookingEvent), not a wrapper around it. SMS enrollment and
the ad-data cohort sync are NOT replicated — SMS is timed against a real
call time this manual path doesn't have (faking one risks texting a
prospect about a call that isn't real), and the cohort sync touches real
ad-spend attribution behind its own approval gate keyed to a real booking
payload. Both are correctness reasons, not "not built yet."

What IS replicated: the actual ESP pre-call enrollment, plus win-back-exit
handling for a prospect currently in an active recovery cadence — skipping
that would be a real bug (they'd get both pre-call and recovery messages),
not a scope choice.

Adds a real, best-effort duplicate-booking check against booking_roster
(refuses unless force:true) and requires the chat layer to always show
preview_pile_on_enrollment's output before calling enroll_in_pile_on.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
